CommitDate: Wed Sep 23 10:49:02 2026 -0500

    fix: LLM escape hatch — --controller-model flag + CRON_CONTROLLER_MODEL env + think-token strip + parse-failure retry (GAP-052)
    
    The controller model was hardcoded to openai/gpt-5.6-luna with no user-reachable
    override, and DeepSeek returns its reasoning INLINE in the content string, so
    json.loads failed on every cycle and controller_plan degraded to a blind ["A"]
    plan (parse_fallback). Either one alone leaves a working provider one hardcoded
    string away but unreachable.
    
    - --controller-model CLI flag + CRON_CONTROLLER_MODEL env (the GAP-049
      POKE_CONTROLLER_MODEL hook still honoured). Precedence: flag > CRON_ > POKE_ >
      default, and the default stays the original luna string, so an invocation with
      neither flag nor env sends a byte-identical request (same model, temperature
      0.3, max_tokens 300, thinking disabled). A *deepseek* model id reaches
      api.deepseek.com through the existing client. The resolved model is printed at
      run start and reported by --dry-run together with the layer it came from.
    - Response parsing: inline <think>...</think> blocks, bare </think>,
      |end_of_thought|-style end markers and trailing stray/partial fragments are
      stripped before parsing, then the first BALANCED JSON object is taken out of
      what remains — the old {[^}]+} regex truncated at the first } and matched
      nothing for a nested object. The marker passes are quote-aware, so a
      marker-shaped substring inside a JSON value survives the strip.
    - When the first answer yields no plan, exactly one retry is made with
      max_tokens + 100 before falling back to the same blind A-press and intent
      labels as before.
    
    Tests: tests/test_gap052_controller_model.py (41 cases, scripted client — no
    network, no live LLM call) covers model precedence, the strip/extract cases and
    the single retry; 28 of them fail against the pre-fix cron_runner.py, and the 13
    that pass are the already-working shapes kept as regression pins. The existing
    tests/test_gap053_decision_intent_summary.py call-count guard now admits the one
    retry — its intent/plan assertions are unchanged.
    
    Verified: ./venv/bin/pytest tests/ -x --tb=short -> 4018 passed, 14 skipped;
    mypy src/ --ignore-missing-imports and mypy cron_runner.py clean; ruff clean;
    cron_runner.py --dry-run with no override prints the pre-GAP-052 line verbatim,
    and with --controller-model / CRON_CONTROLLER_MODEL reports the override.
    
